---
import Feature from "../../layouts/Feature.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"

const faq = [
  {
    q: "How big can a file be?",
    a: "Up to 2 GB per send through any network. In Unlimited mode there is no size limit: the file goes straight between your machines, or through a relay you host. Turn it on per send with <code>--unlimited</code>, or as your default in Settings.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where do my files go on the way?",
    a: "From one machine to the other, encrypted between them. When the two can't connect directly, a relay passes the encrypted bytes along. Nothing is stored in between.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many files can I send at once?",
    a: 'Up to 10 per send. To copy whole folders, use <a href="/features/ssh/">pb rsync or pb scp</a>, which work on every machine with no keys to set up.',
  },
  {
    q: "Can a teammate send files to my machine?",
    a: "Yes. They send a request, and you approve it with <code>pb inbox approve</code> or in the console. A team rule can accept requests from your team automatically.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I get to received files from a browser?",
    a: "Yes. Each machine's page in the web console lists its Inbox, and you can download or remove files there.",
  },
]
---

<Feature
  slug="files"
  title="Send files between machines | Paperboat"
  description="Send files straight to another machine, encrypted end to end. Transfers resume after a drop and are verified."
  headline="Send a file to any machine"
  faq={faq}
  related={["ssh", "console", "self-hosting"]}
  compare={["tailscale", "ssh-bastion"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">Name the file and the machine. It lands in that machine's Inbox, even if the connection drops halfway.</p>
  <Term
    slot="aside"
    lines={["$ pb send report.pdf data.csv --to studio", "✓ report.pdf delivered to studio", "✓ data.csv delivered to studio"]}
  />

  <Beat id="inbox-title" title="It lands in the Inbox">
    <p>Every machine has an Inbox folder. There is no path to type and nothing gets overwritten. Open it in your file manager, or in the console from any browser.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" title="studio" lines={["$ ls ~/Paperboat/Inbox", "data.csv    report.pdf"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="large-title" title="Big files, bad Wi-Fi" flip>
    <p>A send that stops picks up from the last byte that arrived. In Unlimited mode, files of any size go straight from machine to machine.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb send dataset.tar --to gpu-box \\", "    --unlimited", "# the Wi-Fi drops, then comes back", "✓ dataset.tar delivered to gpu-box"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="team-title" title="Files from your team">
    <p>A teammate can ask to send you files. Approve each one, or let your whole team send to your machine.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb inbox requests", "maya   design-v2.fig   38 MB", "$ pb inbox approve r_41k"]} />
  </Beat>

  <section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="details-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="details-title">Details</h2>
      <div class="points points-3">
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Encrypted end to end</h3>
          <p>Only the two machines can read the file. Nothing is kept on a server in between.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Checked on arrival</h3>
          <p>The other machine checks every file before the send counts as done.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">A default machine</h3>
          <p><code>pb send destination set studio</code>, and <code>--to</code> becomes optional.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Feature>
